      "doctor_question": "Hello, I’m Dr. ____. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Hey Doc. Um... well, I came in because I just feel like I got this motor running inside me all day long. It just don't ever shut off. Like, if I have to sit still at church, or out there in the clinic waiting room, or even just sitting around at home, I feel totally trapped. I just have to get up or do something. \n\nWhich is why I was pacing out there by your magazines. You guys have a lot of old magazines, by the way. I saw a Sports Illustrated from like three years ago. The one with the baseball guy on the cover... I used to play baseball when I was a kid. Played shortstop, mostly 'cause you're always moving, you know? Coach said I had good hands but I couldn't ever stay in the dugout without messing with the bats or kicking the dirt. We went to the state championship that year, almost won the whole thing until Jimmy dropped a pop fly. \n\nBut yeah... what was I saying? Right, if I gotta sit still, I just feel trapped. I gotta be moving.",
