    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When you feel that trapped, keyed-up feeling, is your mind also filled with worry most of the time?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Worry? Nah, not really. I mean, it ain't like I'm sitting there fretting about bills or the roof caving in or nothing. It's just... I just gotta move. My legs just want to go. It's like when you wind up one of them little toy cars and you hold the wheels, you know? You can feel it buzzing, just waiting to shoot across the floor. My nephew had one of them, a little red Corvette. We used to race 'em down the hallway at my sister's place. Man, she used to get so mad when we'd hit the baseboards and leave scuff marks. She's got this real nice hardwood floor, oak I think. Or maybe maple? I don't know, it's light colored. But yeah, she'd holler at us to take it outside, but it was raining that day, just pouring down buckets... so what are you gonna do, right? But no, I ain't worried about nothing in particular. Just can't stay put.",
