    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you felt this need to keep moving since you were a child?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh yeah, ever since I was a little kid. Back when I was a boy in school, it was real bad. The teachers, they were always moving my seat around 'cause I just could not stay put for the life of me. I'd be talking out of turn, just blurting stuff out, and I'd always get in big trouble for jumping up out of my chair before class was even done. I'd just be ready to go. \n\nSpeaking of going, you know those old school bells? The big loud metal ones? My granddad had one of those mounted right on his front porch out in the country. He used to yank the rope and ring it when it was time for supper. He lived out on this big piece of land, had like fifty head of cattle... mostly Angus, I think. Black cows, anyway. I used to run around out there chasing the barn cats while everybody else was working. There was this one tomcat, missing half an ear, meanest thing you ever saw. Scratched me right down the arm once when I tried to pick him up near the tractor. Still got the scar... well, it's kind of faded now, but it bled a whole lot. \n\nWhat was I saying? Oh, right, yeah, school. So they'd stick my desk in the back, then move me to the front, then by the window... I liked the window, though. Could watch the cars go by on the highway. But yeah, it's been like this pretty much my whole life.",
